      "value": "@{5ce96ba3134c0b659f14bf3c|full_name}: I just don't want \"trending\" to become another \"new.\" We already have a category for \"new\" and \"hot,\" but we don't have a category showing genuine spikes in relative viewership: what indicates actual trends.\nSay a popular world makes a big change and everyone's checking it out. That should definitely be in trending! Right next to an up-and-coming world that suddenly got a spike in relative visits. Some things take time to build an audience, too, and those worlds shouldn't be left out.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
